      "answer": {
        "lead": "No, it's not too late. Your new-hire enrollment window runs through 2026-11-11, and your Medical PPO election is currently showing as pending. I stopped looking things up early because I hit the tool limit.",
        "policy_facts": [
          {
            "text": "Your records show a Medical PPO election at employee coverage level with status \"pending\", an effective date of 2026-11-01, and an enrollment window ending 2026-11-11. Dental, Vision and 401(k) are also pending. Life is enrolled.",
            "citations": [],
            "data_sources": [
              {
                "tool": "lookup_benefits_status"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "New hires have 30 calendar days from their hire date to enrol in benefits through the HR Portal. Your hire date is 2026-10-12.",
            "citations": [
              {
                "doc_id": "RSE-BEN-01",
                "section": "3.1",
                "snippet": "New hires have 30 calendar days from their hire date to enrol in benefits through the HR Portal."
              }
            ],
            "data_sources": [
              {
                "tool": "lookup_employee_profile"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "If you enrol within your window, coverage is back-dated to the first day of the month after your hire date. Until you enrol, you have no Ridgeline coverage.",
            "citations": [
              {
                "doc_id": "RSE-BEN-01",
                "section": "1.2",
                "snippet": "If you enrol within your new-hire window (\u00a73.1) after that date has passed, your coverage is back-dated to the first day of the month after your hire date."
              },
              {
                "doc_id": "RSE-BEN-01",
                "section": "1.2",
                "snippet": "Until you enrol, you have no Ridgeline coverage, so enrol early in your window."
              }
            ],
            "data_sources": []
          },
          {
            "text": "HR cannot extend the new-hire window. If you miss it, you can next enrol at open enrollment unless you have a qualifying life event before then. This can leave you without Ridgeline coverage until the next plan year.",
            "citations": [
              {
                "doc_id": "RSE-BEN-01",
                "section": "3.2",
                "snippet": "HR cannot extend the new-hire window, so missing it can leave you without Ridgeline coverage until the next plan year."
              }
            ],
            "data_sources": []
          },
          {
            "text": "If you are unsure what to choose, enrol in a plan now. You can change your choices at open enrollment.",
            "citations": [
              {
                "doc_id": "RSE-BEN-01",
                "section": "3.2",
                "snippet": "If you are close to the end of your window and unsure what to choose, enrol in a plan now; you can change your choices at open enrollment."
              }
            ],
            "data_sources": []
          }
        ],
        "recommendations": [
          {
            "text": "Log in to the HR Portal under Benefits and confirm your Medical PPO choice well before 2026-11-11. Your election shows as pending, so check that it was actually submitted."
          },
          {
            "text": "If the portal doesn't show your election as complete, contact the HR Service Desk. I can open an HR ticket for you if you'd like."
          }
        ]
      },
