            "output": {
              "passages": [
                {
                  "doc_id": "RSE-BEN-01",
                  "title": "Benefits Summary & Eligibility",
                  "section": "3.2",
                  "section_heading": "If you miss the window",
                  "text": "If you miss your new-hire window, you can next enrol at open enrollment, unless you have a qualifying life event (\u00a73.4) before then.\nHR cannot extend the new-hire window, so missing it can leave you without Ridgeline coverage until the next plan year. If you are close to the end of your window and unsure what to choose, enrol in a plan now; you can change your choices at open enrollment.",
                  "score": 0.0323
                },
                {
                  "doc_id": "RSE-ONB-01",
                  "title": "Onboarding Procedures",
                  "section": "2.3",
                  "section_heading": "Benefits enrollment",
                  "text": "You have a 30-day window from your hire date to enrol in benefits; see RSE-BEN-01 \u00a73.1. Don't leave it to the last week.",
                  "score": 0.0323
                },
                {
                  "doc_id": "RSE-BEN-01",
                  "title": "Benefits Summary & Eligibility",
                  "section": "3.1",
                  "section_heading": "New hires",
                  "text": "New hires have 30 calendar days from their hire date to enrol in benefits through the HR Portal. For example, an employee hired on October 12 can enrol until November 11. Coverage starts as described in \u00a71.2.\nEnrol in the HR Portal under Benefits. Choose your plans and coverage levels, add any family members you want to cover, and confirm. If you don't want a plan, you can waive it. Your choices then apply for the rest of the plan year.",
                  "score": 0.0318
                },
                {
                  "doc_id": "RSE-BEN-01",
                  "title": "Benefits Summary & Eligibility",
                  "section": "1.2",
                  "section_heading": "When coverage starts",
                  "text": "Coverage starts on the first day of the month after your hire date. If you enrol within your new-hire window (\u00a73.1) after that date has passed, your coverage is back-dated to the first day of the month after your hire date.\nFor example, an employee hired in the middle of October is covered from the first day of November once they enrol, even if they enrol a few days into November. Until you enrol, you have no Ridgeline coverage, so enrol early in your window.",
                  "score": 0.0315
                },
                {
                  "doc_id": "RSE-BEN-01",
                  "title": "Benefits Summary & Eligibility",
                  "section": "3.3",
                  "section_heading": "Open enrollment",
                  "text": "Open enrollment for 2027 runs from November 16 to November 30, 2026. Choices made at open enrollment take effect on January 1, 2027. Open enrollment is the time to join, change or leave a plan for the coming year.\nHR sends a reminder before open enrollment starts, with any changes to the plans for the coming year. If you make no changes, your current elections generally continue into the new year. Check your family members and coverage levels each year.",
                  "score": 0.031
                }
              ],
              "evidence": "ok"
